> assistant
The left editor was getting focus because `window.activeTextEditor` doesn't always update right after `workbench.action.splitEditorRight`. The target column was read before VS Code switched the active editor, so it pointed at the left group. Applying the layout could also shift group numbers.

The fix focuses the last (right) editor group after the layout is applied. It then shows the document in that active group, so the right editor gets focus. This works for both a new split and a reused one.

